arXiv:2509.22633v1 [stat.ML] 26 Sep 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line" lang="en">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human
Feedback</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Gen Li
</span><span id="id1" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_note ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span>Department of Statistics and Data Science, The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Hong
Kong; Email: <span id="id1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">genli@cuhk.edu.hk</span>.</span></span></span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_note"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Note: </span>The authors contributed equally.
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Yuling Yan<span id="footnotex1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnotemark"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">footnotemark: </span>
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
          
          
          
        </span></span></span>
</span><span id="id2" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_note ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span>Department of Statistics, University of Wisconsin-Madison, WI 53706,
USA; Email: <span id="id2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">yuling.yan@wisc.edu</span>.</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Reinforcement learning with human feedback (RLHF), which learns a reward model from human preference data and then optimizes a policy to favor preferred responses, has emerged as a central paradigm for aligning large language models (LLMs) with human preferences. In this paper, we investigate exploration principles for online RLHF, where one seeks to adaptively collect new preference data to refine both the reward model and the policy in a data-efficient manner. By examining existing optimism-based exploration algorithms, we identify a drawback in their sampling protocol: they tend to gather comparisons that fail to reduce the most informative uncertainties in reward differences, and we prove lower bounds showing that such methods can incur linear regret over exponentially long horizons. Motivated by this insight, we propose a new exploration scheme that directs preference queries toward reducing uncertainty in reward differences most relevant to policy improvement. Under a multi-armed bandit model of RLHF, we establish regret bounds of order <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{(\beta+1)/(\beta+2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{(\beta+1)/(\beta+2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperparameter that balances reward maximization against mitigating distribution shift. To our knowledge, this is the first online RLHF algorithm with regret scaling polynomially in all model parameters.</p>
  
</div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Keywords:</span> Reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF), online exploration, principle of optimism, preference data</p>
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable capabilities across a wide range of natural language tasks, yet aligning their behavior with human preferences remains a central challenge. A widely adopted solution is reinforcement learning with human feedback (RLHF), which fine-tunes a pretrained LLM using human preference data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christiano et al.,, 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ziegler et al.,, 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al.,, 2022</a>)</cite>. The standard RLHF pipeline involves three stages: (i) supervised fine-tuning (SFT) on human-written demonstrations to produce a baseline model; (ii) training a reward model from human preference comparisons <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bradley and Terry,, 1952</a>)</cite>; and (iii) optimizing the LLM with reinforcement learning against the learned reward. This framework has been instrumental in the success of instruction-following LLMs such as InstructGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al.,, 2022</a>)</cite> and ChatGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI,, 2023</a>)</cite>, enabling models to produce responses that are more helpful, safe, and aligned with human expectations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite this progress, most existing RLHF implementations are offline <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al.,, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al.,, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite>: the preference data is collected once from static policies, and the reward model is trained on this fixed dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ivison et al.,, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al.,, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>. While effective, offline RLHF has inherent limitations—It cannot adaptively explore the enormous space of natural language, leading to inefficient use of expensive human feedback. In contrast, online RLHF offers a more powerful alternative: the policy iteratively collects new preference data, updates the reward model, and improves itself based on these updates <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al.,, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al.,, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al.,, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rosset et al.,, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al.,, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Feng et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>. This interactive loop has the potential to greatly improve both alignment quality and sample efficiency. However, realizing this potential requires principled approaches to exploration, i.e., deciding which comparisons to query in order to most effectively reduce uncertainty in reward estimation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A natural candidate for encouraging and guiding exploration is the principle of optimism <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lai and Robbins,, 1985</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lattimore and Szepesvári,, 2020</a>)</cite>, which acts as if the environment is more optimistic than currently estimated, within the limits of statistical uncertainty based on all data that has been observed so far. It is usually implemented by adding an uncertainty-based bonus to reward or value estimates, thereby prioritizing actions whose values are uncertain but potentially high. This has yielded provably efficient algorithms in standard RL (see e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., (2018)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zanette and Brunskill, (2019)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Russo and Van Roy, (2013)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., (2017)</a></cite>).
However, extending this principle to RLHF introduces new difficulties, where feedback comes not as a single reward but as a difference between rewards of two actions. The key challenge is to determine the action pairs with the large uncertainties most relevant to policy improvement.
A few recent works achieved important progress towards designing sample-efficient online RLHF algorithms based on the optimism principle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cen et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>. However the existing theoretical guarantees still exhibit exponential dependency on certain model parameters, which potentially leads to inefficient exploration.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With this context, this paper makes contribution towards designing efficient online exploration schemes for RLHF with provable guarantees. By analyzing the existing algorithms in the seminal works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cen et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>, we discuss their inadequacy in exploring the action pairs with the large uncertainties most relevant to policy improvement, and construct lower bounds to show that the exponential dependency on certain parameters is unavoidable in their regret. Based on these insights, we propose a new exploration scheme for RLHF that adopts a different sampling protocol, and establish a regret bound that depends polynomially on all model parameters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Model set-up</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Preliminaries.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In RLHF, the prompt space <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the collection
of all possible inputs or queries that a user might provide to the
model. The answer (or action) space <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of all possible
outputs the model can generate in reply to a given prompt. A language
model is a policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:\mathcal{X}\to\Delta(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:\mathcal{X}\to\Delta(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math> that defines
a probability distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot\,|\,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot\,|\,x)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>
conditioned on a prompt <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, specifying how likely
the model is to produce each potential response.
The pipeline of RLHF starts with supervised fine-tuning (SFT), where a reference policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}:\mathcal{X}\to\Delta(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}:\mathcal{X}\to\Delta(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by fine-tuning a pre-trained LLM on a dataset of prompts paired with high-quality answers written by humans. SVT provides an initialization that stabilizes and improves the effectiveness of the subsequent training stages that aligns the LLM with human preferences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward modeling.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To translate human preferences into a trainable objective, one need
to model how an oracle (e.g., a human annotator) rank two answers
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> given prompt <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Following a line of prior
works (e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cen et al., (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al., (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., (2025)</a></cite>),
we assume that preferences follow the Bradley-Terry model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bradley and Terry,, 1952</a>)</cite></p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(a_{1}\succ a_{2}\,|\,x)=\frac{\exp(r^{\star}(x,a_{1}))}{\exp(r^{\star}(x,a_{1}))+\exp(r^{\star}(x,a_{2}))}=\sigma\left(r^{\star}(x,a_{1})-r^{\star}(x,a_{2})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(a_{1}\succ a_{2}\,|\,x)=\frac{\exp(r^{\star}(x,a_{1}))}{\exp(r^{\star}(x,a_{1}))+\exp(r^{\star}(x,a_{2}))}=\sigma\left(r^{\star}(x,a_{1})-r^{\star}(x,a_{2})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> is an
underlying reward function of an answer given a prompt, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}\succ a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}\succ a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
means the answer <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is preferred compared to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(x)=(1+e^{-x})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(x)=(1+e^{-x})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the sigmoid function. We also define a policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}</annotation></semantics></math>
to characterize human preference:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a\,|\,x)=\frac{\exp(r^{\star}(x,a))}{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\exp(r^{\star}(x,a^{\prime}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a\,|\,x)=\frac{\exp(r^{\star}(x,a))}{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\exp(r^{\star}(x,a^{\prime}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The reward function is unknown and can be learned from e.g., an offline
dataset <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(x^{i},a_{+}^{i},a_{-}^{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(x^{i},a_{+}^{i},a_{-}^{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math> comprised of
independent preference data samples using maximum likelihood estimation
(MLE):</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\arg\max}_{r}\ell(r,\mathcal{D})\quad\text{where}\quad\ell(r,\mathcal{D})\coloneqq\sum_{\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma\big(r(x^{i},a_{+}^{i})-r(x^{i},a_{-}^{i})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\arg\max}_{r}\ell(r,\mathcal{D})\quad\text{where}\quad\ell(r,\mathcal{D})\coloneqq\sum_{\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma\big(r(x^{i},a_{+}^{i})-r(x^{i},a_{-}^{i})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where a preference data sample denoted by <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> means
that <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{+}\succ a_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{+}\succ a_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> given prompt <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RL fine-tuning.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a reward model <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, we seek to fine-tune the policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>
to balance reward maximization with maintaining similarity to the
original model <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the SFT stage. Towards this,
we define the KL-regularized reward objective</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho}\big[\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi(\cdot\,|\,x)}[r(x,a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(\cdot\,|\,x)}[r(x,a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}\big(\pi(\cdot\,|\,x)\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(\cdot\,|\,x)\big)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho}\big[\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi(\cdot\,|\,x)}[r(x,a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(\cdot\,|\,x)}[r(x,a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}\big(\pi(\cdot\,|\,x)\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(\cdot\,|\,x)\big)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is the prompt distribution, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the regularization
parameter reflecting the strength of the KL regularization. In practice, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is typically chosen to be small; for instance, in InstructGPT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al.,, 2022</a>)</cite> the optimal value is reported to be around <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.02</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.02</annotation></semantics></math>. This objective function includes a calibration policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>
to eliminate the shift ambiguity of the reward function, as two reward
functions <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,a)+c(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,a)+c(x)</annotation></semantics></math> lead to the same preference
model (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In Reward modeling. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>). Given any reward function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>,
the optimal policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r}\coloneqq\arg\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r}\coloneqq\arg\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math>
admits a closed-form expression <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite></p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r}(a\,|\,x)=\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a\,|\,x)\exp(r(x,a)/\beta)}{Z_{r}(x)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r}(a\,|\,x)=\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a\,|\,x)\exp(r(x,a)/\beta)}{Z_{r}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{r}(x)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a|x)\exp(r(x,a)/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{r}(x)=\sum_{a}\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a|x)\exp(r(x,a)/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>
is the normalizing factor. Notice that the selection of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>
does not affect the optimal policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> given the reward function
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. Our target is the optimal policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes
the objective (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In RL fine-tuning. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>) under the true reward function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>,
namely</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}\coloneqq\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}\coloneqq\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Offline RLHF.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The above framework leads to offline RLHF methods that relies on the
preference dataset <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> for training. Initial approaches
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christiano et al.,, 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al.,, 2022</a>)</cite> first estimate a reward
function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the preference dataset <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>
using MLE, then optimize the KL-regularized objective (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In RL fine-tuning. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>)
with respect to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Another approach introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., (2024)</a></cite>
condensed these two steps into one single step, known as direct preference
optimization (DPO), which optimizes</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi}\sum_{\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma\bigg(\beta\Big(\log\frac{\pi(y_{+}^{i}\,|\,x)}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(y_{+}^{i}\,|\,x)}-\log\frac{\pi(y_{-}^{i}\,|\,x)}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(y_{-}^{i}\,|\,x)}\Big)\bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>π</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi}\sum_{\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma\bigg(\beta\Big(\log\frac{\pi(y_{+}^{i}\,|\,x)}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(y_{+}^{i}\,|\,x)}-\log\frac{\pi(y_{-}^{i}\,|\,x)}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(y_{-}^{i}\,|\,x)}\Big)\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The above objective avoids explicitly estimating the reward function,
which can be obtained by expressing the reward function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> in the
MLE formulation (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In Reward modeling. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>) with the associated optimal policy
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> using the closed-form expression (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In RL fine-tuning. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>).
However, as discussed in e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al., (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., (2025)</a></cite>,
the efficiency of offline RLHF is limited by the coverage of the offline
dataset <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and online exploration with active data collection
is necessary to achieve sample efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Online RLHF.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider reward learning and policy learning iteratively, where
in the <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration we use the current policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, obtained
from previous iterations, to sample new data and subsequently update
both the reward estimate and the policy. This setup enables online
exploration in RLHF by refining the reward model and policy in tandem
as new preference data is collected. We aim to minimize the regret</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(T)\coloneqq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\big[J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(T)\coloneqq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\big[J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It is worth mentioning that the choice of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math> does
not affect the regret. We define the following function <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>
that measures the optimal objective value for a given reward <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\coloneqq\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})=J(\pi_{r},r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\coloneqq\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})=J(\pi_{r},r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This function plays an important role in the exploration algorithms.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>RLHF with online exploration</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Three recent algorithms for online RLHF are most closely related to this work: VPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cen et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>, XPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>, and SELM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>. In this section, we first analyze and discuss these approaches, and then introduce our proposed exploration scheme.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Inadequacy of existing approaches</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by reviewing the procedure and intuition behind VPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cen et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>.
Fix a calibration policy <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math> and an initial policy <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\ldots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\ldots,T</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration of VPO consists of the following steps:</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample a prompt <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{t}\sim\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{t}\sim\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and two answers <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1}^{t},a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}(\cdot\,|\,x^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{t},a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}(\cdot\,|\,x^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Query the preference oracle to obtain pairwise comparison <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{+}^{t}\succ a_{-}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{+}^{t}\succ a_{-}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Update the preference dataset <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{(t)}=\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)}\cup\{(x^{t},a_{+}^{t},a_{-}^{t})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{(t)}=\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)}\cup\{(x^{t},a_{+}^{t},a_{-}^{t})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Update the reward model <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and the policy <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>
using the updated preference dataset <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E1.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{r:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{r:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t+1)};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t+1)};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.1b)</span></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left" style="white-space:normal;" colspan="5">where <math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a regularization parameter, and step (<a href="#S3.E1.2" title="In 3.1 ‣ item 2 ‣ 3.1 Inadequacy of existing approaches ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1b</span></a>)
admits closed-form solution (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In RL fine-tuning. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>).</td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To illustrate the rationale behind VPO, consider the bandit case with no prompt. Step (<a href="#S3.E1.1" title="In 3.1 ‣ item 2 ‣ 3.1 Inadequacy of existing approaches ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1a</span></a>) applies the optimism principle, encouraging exploration based on the uncertainty in estimating the reward difference between each action <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and the calibration policy <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Formally, it can be viewed as the Lagrangian form of the constrained optimization problem</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{r,\pi}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[r(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\geq\max_{r}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-B" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{r,\pi}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[r(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\geq\max_{r}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. After the change of variable <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}(a)=r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(a)=r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]</annotation></semantics></math>, this becomes</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{r^{\prime},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[r^{\prime}(a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\ell(r^{\prime},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\geq\max_{r^{\prime}}\ell(r^{\prime},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-B,\quad\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r^{\prime}(a)]=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{r^{\prime},\pi}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[r^{\prime}(a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\ell(r^{\prime},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\geq\max_{r^{\prime}}\ell(r^{\prime},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-B,\quad\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r^{\prime}(a)]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Here, the constraint set can be interpreted as a confidence region reflecting the uncertainty in estimating each <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the updated policy <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> depends both on the true reward gap <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]</annotation></semantics></math> and on the uncertainty in estimating this gap for each action <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For intuition, suppose <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}=\ind_{a_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝟙</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}=\ind_{a_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume that the true reward gaps are small. In this case, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> favors actions with higher estimation uncertainty relative to <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., those <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> where the estimate of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a)-r(a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a)-r(a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is most uncertain. However, comparing two actions <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},a_{2}\sim\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},a_{2}\sim\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces the uncertainty between them, rather than the (potentially larger) uncertainty relative to <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. This misalignment can lead to inefficient exploration, as illustrated in the following example.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 1</span></span><span id="Thmexample1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the bandit setting with three actions <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{a_{0},a_{1},a_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{a_{0},a_{1},a_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the true rewards are <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(a_{0})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(a_{0})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(a_{1})=r^{\star}(a_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(a_{1})=r^{\star}(a_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the reference policy <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> be uniform over <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the calibration policy be <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(a_{1})=\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(a_{2})=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(a_{1})=\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(a_{2})=p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(a_{0})=1-2p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}(a_{0})=1-2p</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmexample1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq p&lt;1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq p&lt;1/4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following proposition shows that VPO may fail to explore efficiently in this setting The proof can be found in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmprop1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmprop1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmprop1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmprop1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmprop1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the setup in Example <a href="#Thmexample1" title="Example 1. ‣ 3.1 Inadequacy of existing approaches ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Let the initial policy <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> of VPO be the uniform distribution
over <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}/\beta\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}/\beta\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least
<math id="Thmprop1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4/(9e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4/(9e)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\geq\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})\geq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmprop1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">holds for any <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;t\leq\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;t\leq\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let’s discuss the idea behind Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Inadequacy of existing approaches ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}=\ind_{a_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝟙</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}=\ind_{a_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If the calibration action <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is not visited during the first <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, then <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> will continue to favor <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, since both gaps <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{1})-r(a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{1})-r(a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{2})-r(a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{2})-r(a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> remain highly uncertain. In particular, we establish that <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})\leq\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})\leq\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is exponentially small, implying that <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is unlikely to
be sampled in iteration <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, with constant probability, <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> will not be sampled within the first <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\exp(r_{\max}/\beta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\exp(r_{\max}/\beta))</annotation></semantics></math> iterations, and the resulting highly suboptimal policy incurs linear regret over an exponentially long horizon. This example highlights an algorithmic drawback: although VPO acknowledges uncertainty in the reward gaps between <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (and between <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>), it continues to encourage sampling <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, leading primarily to comparisons between them that fail to reduce their uncertainty relative to <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Uncertainty-based RLHF exploration.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> initial policies <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(0)},\pi^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(0)},\pi^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, regularizaton parameters <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{t}\}_{t\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{t}\}_{t\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.4.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.4.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.4.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            Sample a prompt <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{t}\sim\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{t}\sim\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and two answers <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t-1)}(\cdot\,|\,x^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t-1)}(\cdot\,|\,x^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}(\cdot\,|\,x^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}(\cdot\,|\,x^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            Query the preference oracle to obtain pairwise comparison <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{+}^{t}\succ a_{-}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{+}^{t}\succ a_{-}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and update the preference dataset <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{(t)}=\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)}\cup\{(x^{t},a_{+}^{t},a_{-}^{t})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{(t)}=\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)}\cup\{(x^{t},a_{+}^{t},a_{-}^{t})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            Update the reward model <math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and the policy <math id="alg1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>
using <math id="alg1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>:

<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="6"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E2.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell">
                          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_td"><span id="S3.E2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
                        </td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{r:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r;\pi^{(t)})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{r:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r;\pi^{(t)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.2a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E2.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t+1)};\pi^{(t)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t+1)};\pi^{(t)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3.2b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            where the policy update (<a href="#S3.E2.2" title="In 3.2 ‣ 6 ‣ 1 ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2b</span></a>) admits closed-form solution (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In RL fine-tuning. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            <span id="alg1.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> <math id="alg1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi^{(t)}:1\leq t\leq T\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi^{(t)}:1\leq t\leq T\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A natural modification to address the issue above is to change the sampling scheme so that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The intuition is that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> encourages to explore actions with
higher estimation uncertainty relative to the actions favored by the
calibration policy <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To effectively reduce this
uncertainty, it is sensible to compare one action drawn from <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>
with another drawn from <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, the XPO
and SELM algorithms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite> can be viewed
as taking <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}=\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}=\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, if the fixed calibration policy <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math> is highly suboptimal for reward maximization (for example, if it concentrates on a few low-reward actions), then the comparison will almost always favor <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> against <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
yielding little useful information. This issue is illustrated in the following example.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 2</span></span><span id="Thmexample2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the bandit setting with three actions <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{a_{0},a_{1},a_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{a_{0},a_{1},a_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the true rewards are <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(a_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(a_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(a_{1})=r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(a_{1})=r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(a_{2})=r_{\max}-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(a_{2})=r_{\max}-2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the reference policy be <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{0})=1-2/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{0})=1-2/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{1})=\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{2})=1/\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{1})=\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{2})=1/\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geq 4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following result shows that, when <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is large (as we will see in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, this corresponds to the case where the reference policy deviates from human preference), this modified sampling schemes can lead to inefficient exploration in this setting. The proof is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmprop2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmprop2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmprop2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmprop2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmprop2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the setup in Example <a href="#Thmexample2" title="Example 2. ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Assume that <math id="Thmprop2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmprop2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\leq\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\leq\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any initial policy <math id="Thmprop2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmprop2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least
<math id="Thmprop2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/64</annotation></semantics></math>, the modified exploration scheme which samples <math id="Thmprop2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmprop2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\geq 0.01" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\geq 0.01</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmprop2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="Thmprop2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;t\leq\min\{\kappa,\exp(r_{\max})/2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;t\leq\min\{\kappa,\exp(r_{\max})/2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This lower bound suggests that relying on a fixed calibration policy can lead to inefficient exploration over an exponentially long horizon. We will come back to this example in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> after presenting our algorithm and theoretical guarantees. This observation motivates us to update the calibration policy in each iteration adaptively.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Uncertainty-based exploration.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose an exploration scheme where the calibration policy evolves with the iterations. In the <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration, instead of a fixed <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>
, we use <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> as the calibration policy when optimizing <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E3.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.x1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{r:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r;\pi^{(t)})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{r:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]}\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r;\pi^{(t)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E3.x2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.x2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.x2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t+1)};\pi^{(t)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathop{\arg\max}_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t+1)};\pi^{(t)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The key advantage is that <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> improves over time, guiding exploration away from uninformative comparisons. Since <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> emphasizes actions with higher uncertainty relative to <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is natural to compare <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}^{t}\sim\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields preference data that more directly reduces uncertainty, leading to more efficient exploration. Our full exploration scheme is summarized in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Theoretical results</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We establish theoretical guarantees for Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> under the multi-armed bandit setting
(i.e., <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>) with <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=|\mathcal{A}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=|\mathcal{A}|</annotation></semantics></math>. We begin
with a general regret bound, whose proof is deferred to Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}&gt;A\log T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}&gt;A\log T</annotation></semantics></math> be non-decreasing in <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a universal constant <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, with probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(T^{-10})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(T^{-10})</annotation></semantics></math>, the cumulative regret of running Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> iterations satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(T)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq Cr_{\mathsf{max}}A^{2}\sqrt{T\log T}+C\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T}{\alpha_{t}}+CA^{2}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq Cr_{\mathsf{max}}A^{2}\sqrt{T\log T}+C\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T}{\alpha_{t}}+CA^{2}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+C(r_{\mathsf{max}}+\log T)\hskip-8.61108pt\sum_{r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})}\hskip-8.61108pt\min\bigg\{\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}},\left(T\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\right)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+1}}\alpha_{T}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}r_{\max}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}\bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>T</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+C(r_{\mathsf{max}}+\log T)\hskip-8.61108pt\sum_{r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})}\hskip-8.61108pt\min\bigg\{\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}},\left(T\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\right)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+1}}\alpha_{T}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}r_{\max}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}\bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now discuss the implications of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. When
<math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to the case where only reward maximization
matters, the regret bound (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>) simplifies to</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(T)=\widetilde{O}\big((A^{3/2}r_{\max}^{3/2}+A^{2}r_{\max})\sqrt{T}\big)\qquad\text{when}\qquad\alpha_{t}\asymp A\log T+\sqrt{\frac{t}{Ar_{\max}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>when</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(T)=\widetilde{O}\big((A^{3/2}r_{\max}^{3/2}+A^{2}r_{\max})\sqrt{T}\big)\qquad\text{when}\qquad\alpha_{t}\asymp A\log T+\sqrt{\frac{t}{Ar_{\max}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the performance of the exploration algorithm becomes
more intricate due to the trade-off between reward maximization and
similarity to the reference policy. To interpret the general regret
bound in this regime, we introduce the following assumption to capture
the interaction between human preference <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
the reference policy <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa,\tau\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa,\tau\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>
such that, for any action pair <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\geq\tau\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}\geq\kappa^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\geq\tau\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}\geq\kappa^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> requires that whenever
<math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is substantially more preferred than <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> under human
preference, the reference policy does not assign disproportionately
higher weight to <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> than to <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is reasonable, since
<math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained from the SFT step, where a pretrained
LLM is fine-tuned on human demonstrations already broadly aligned
with preference. The quantities <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> capture the degree of alignment between <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and their size reflects the influence of the reference policy on RLHF. We note that the illustrative Example <a href="#Thmexample1" title="Example 1. ‣ 3.1 Inadequacy of existing approaches ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> satisfies Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with <math id="S4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa,\tau=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa,\tau=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the parameter <math id="S4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> in Example <a href="#Thmexample2" title="Example 2. ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is consistent with the <math id="S4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> here. Under this assumption, we obtain the following simplified regret bound, whose proof is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmprop3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmprop3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmprop3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmprop3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmprop3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
holds. Let</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=A\log T+t^{\frac{1}{\beta+2}}\Big(\frac{r_{\max}}{\kappa}\Big)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+2}}\Big(\frac{\log T}{A(r_{\max}+\log T)}\Big)^{\frac{\beta+1}{\beta+2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=A\log T+t^{\frac{1}{\beta+2}}\Big(\frac{r_{\max}}{\kappa}\Big)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+2}}\Big(\frac{\log T}{A(r_{\max}+\log T)}\Big)^{\frac{\beta+1}{\beta+2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmprop3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then with probability at least <math id="Thmprop3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(T^{-10})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(T^{-10})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(T)\lesssim(\tau+\kappa^{\beta}T^{\frac{\beta+1}{\beta+2}})\,\mathsf{poly}(A,r_{\max},\log T)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝗉𝗈𝗅𝗒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(T)\lesssim(\tau+\kappa^{\beta}T^{\frac{\beta+1}{\beta+2}})\,\mathsf{poly}(A,r_{\max},\log T),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmprop3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the degree of the polynomial factor does not depend on <math id="Thmprop3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Remark</span><span id="Thmremark1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is large, namely the reference policy deviates significantly from the human preference, it is natural to choose a small KL regularization parameter <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> to reduce the influence of the reference policy. In this regime, Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> remains robust, since the regret bound scales only with <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. By contrast, the lower bound in Proposition <a href="#Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> suggests that the sampling protocols in prior works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite> would incur regret at least linear in <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. This demonstrates that our strategy accommodates scenarios with small <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, where the reference policy is poorly aligned with human preference.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Remark</span><span id="Thmremark2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Another assumption and the regret bound ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, we present an alternative
assumption linking human preference and the reference policy, together with the corresponding regret guarantee.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#Thmprop3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> establishes a regret bound of order
<math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{\frac{\beta+1}{\beta+2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{\frac{\beta+1}{\beta+2}})</annotation></semantics></math>, with only polynomial dependence
on the other parameters. This stands in sharp contrast to prior works
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cen et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al.,, 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>,
which achieved the more standard <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{T})</annotation></semantics></math> regret but at the
cost of exponential dependence on terms such as <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
We conjecture that, for RLHF, eliminating exponential dependence inevitably
requires a slower rate in <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, with the exponent governed by <math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
This trade-off is intuitive: online exploration primarily serves to
learn human preference, and as the regularization parameter <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>
increases, greater emphasis is placed on preserving similarity to
the reference measure. This constraint naturally slows convergence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> </h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Step 1: regret decomposition</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In view of the optimality of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. equation (<a href="#S3.E2.1" title="In 3.2 ‣ 6 ‣ 1 ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2a</span></a>)),
we have</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})\geq\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})\geq\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})+\alpha_{t}J^{\star}(r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Rearrange terms to get</p>
<table id="S5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}}\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}}\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq J^{\star}(r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J^{\star}(r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq J^{\star}(r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J^{\star}(r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{(i)}}{=}\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(i)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{(i)}}{=}\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(ii)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here step (i) follows from the definition of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. equation
(<a href="#S2.E7" title="In Online RLHF. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.7</span></a>)), while step (ii) follows from the optimality
of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. equation (<a href="#S3.E2.2" title="In 3.2 ‣ 6 ‣ 1 ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2b</span></a>)). This allows
us to reach the following decomposition:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{Regret}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀𝗋𝖾𝗍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{Regret}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq J(\pi^{\star},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{\alpha_{t}^{-1}\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\big]}_{\eqqcolon\theta_{t}}+\underbrace{J(\pi^{(t)},r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})}_{\eqqcolon\gamma_{t}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{\alpha_{t}^{-1}\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\big]}_{\eqqcolon\theta_{t}}+\underbrace{J(\pi^{(t)},r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})}_{\eqqcolon\gamma_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In view of the definition of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. equation (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In RL fine-tuning. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>)),
we can further decompose</p>
<table id="S5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{\star}(a)]+\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{\star}(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{\star}(a)]+\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{\star}(a)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{t})-r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{t})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{t})+r^{\star}(a_{1}^{t})+\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{t})-r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{t})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{t})+r^{\star}(a_{1}^{t})+\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the martingale difference sequence</p>
<table id="S5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]-r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{t})-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]+r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]-r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{t})-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{(t)}(a)]+r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{\star}(a)]+r^{\star}(a_{2}^{t})+\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{\star}(a)]-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{\star}(a)]+r^{\star}(a_{2}^{t})+\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{\star}(a)]-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore we have</p>
<table id="S5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Regret}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathsf{Regret}_{t}\leq\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\theta_{t}}_{\eqqcolon\theta}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\xi_{t}}_{\eqqcolon\xi}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}|r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{t})-r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{t})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{t})+r^{\star}(a_{1}^{t})|}_{\eqqcolon\zeta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀𝗋𝖾𝗍</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀𝗋𝖾𝗍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Regret}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathsf{Regret}_{t}\leq\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\theta_{t}}_{\eqqcolon\theta}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}\xi_{t}}_{\eqqcolon\xi}+\underbrace{\sum_{t=1}^{T}|r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{t})-r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{t})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{t})+r^{\star}(a_{1}^{t})|}_{\eqqcolon\zeta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to bound the second term <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that
<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\xi_{t}|\leq 8r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\xi_{t}|\leq 8r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> holds deterministically for any <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the Azuma-Hoeffding inequality, with probability exceeding <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(T^{-10})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(T^{-10})</annotation></semantics></math>
we have</p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\xi_{t}\leq C_{1}r_{\mathsf{max}}\sqrt{T\log T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\xi_{t}\leq C_{1}r_{\mathsf{max}}\sqrt{T\log T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">for some universal constant <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In what follows, we bound
the other two terms <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Step 2: bounding likelihood ratios</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To bound <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to analyze the regularized MLE. Notice
that</p>
<table id="S5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}=\frac{\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})}{\alpha_{t}}=\alpha_{t}^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{(t)}(x^{i},a_{+}^{i})-r^{(t)}(x^{i},a_{-}^{i}))}{\sigma(r^{\star}(x^{i},a_{+}^{i})-r^{\star}(x^{i},a_{-}^{i}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}=\frac{\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})}{\alpha_{t}}=\alpha_{t}^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{(t)}(x^{i},a_{+}^{i})-r^{(t)}(x^{i},a_{-}^{i}))}{\sigma(r^{\star}(x^{i},a_{+}^{i})-r^{\star}(x^{i},a_{-}^{i}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The following lemma is crucial for the subsequent analysis. The proof can be found in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof of auxiliary lemmas ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any given reward function
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{t}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{t}(r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{-}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{+}^{i})-r(a_{-}^{i}))}-\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{-}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{+}^{i})-r(a_{-}^{i}))}-\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists some universal constant <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any
fixed <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta_{t}(r)|\leq C_{2}\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{t}r_{\mathsf{max}}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big)\log\frac{\log T}{\delta}}+C_{2}r_{\mathsf{max}}\log\frac{\log t}{\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta_{t}(r)|\leq C_{2}\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{t}r_{\mathsf{max}}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big)\log\frac{\log T}{\delta}}+C_{2}r_{\mathsf{max}}\log\frac{\log t}{\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Equipped with the concentration bounds in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 5.2 Step 2: bounding likelihood ratios ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
we can use the standard covering argument to derive an uniform upper
bound, whose proof is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof of auxiliary lemmas ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists some universal constant
<math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that with probability exceeding <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(T^{-9})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(T^{-9})</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\leq-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big)+C_{3}Ar_{\max}\log T" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\leq-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big)+C_{3}Ar_{\max}\log T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">holds for any <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:\mathcal{A}\to[0,r_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As an immediate consequence of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 5.2 Step 2: bounding likelihood ratios ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, with
probability exceeding <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(T^{-9})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(T^{-9})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\leq C_{3}Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\leq C_{3}Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">holds for any <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</p>
<table id="S5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\theta_{t}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})}{\alpha_{t}}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{C_{3}Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T}{\alpha_{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\theta_{t}=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})}{\alpha_{t}}\leq\sum_{t=1}^{T}\frac{C_{3}Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T}{\alpha_{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Step 3: bounding reward errors</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first notice that</p>
<table id="S5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{t}^{-1}\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{t}^{-1}\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t-1)})\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{(i)}}{\geq}\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(i)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{(i)}}{\geq}\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-\max_{\pi}J(\pi,r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(ii)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}J(\pi^{(t)},r^{\star};\pi^{(t-1)})-J(\pi^{(t)},r^{(t)};\pi^{(t-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{(iii)}}{=}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{(t)}(a)-r^{\star}(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{(t)}(a)-r^{\star}(a)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(iii)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{(iii)}}{=}\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t)}}[r^{(t)}(a)-r^{\star}(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi^{(t-1)}}[r^{(t)}(a)-r^{\star}(a)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-4r_{\max}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-4r_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here step (i) is an intermediate step of (<a href="#S5.E1" title="In 5.1 Step 1: regret decomposition ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>);
step (ii) follows from the optimality of <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. (<a href="#S3.E2.2" title="In 3.2 ‣ 6 ‣ 1 ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2b</span></a>));
step (iii) follows from the definition of <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> (cf. (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In RL fine-tuning. ‣ 2 Model set-up ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>)).
This combined with Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 5.2 Step 2: bounding likelihood ratios ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> implies that</p>
<table id="S5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{i}))\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{t}\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r^{(t)}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{(t)}(a_{2}^{i}))\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq-2\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\big]+2C_{3}Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T\leq C_{4}\alpha_{t}r_{\max}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq-2\big[\ell(r^{(t)},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})-\ell(r^{\star},\mathcal{D}^{(t)})\big]+2C_{3}Ar_{\mathsf{max}}\log T\leq C_{4}\alpha_{t}r_{\max},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">as long as <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\geq A\log T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\geq A\log T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{4}\geq 8+2C_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{4}\geq 8+2C_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. This
implies that for any <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[T]</annotation></semantics></math> and any action pair <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+})-r^{\star}(a_{-}))\|\sigma(r^{(t)}(a_{+})-r^{(t)}(a_{-}))\big)\leq\frac{C_{4}\alpha_{t}r_{\max}}{N_{t}(a_{+},a_{-})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+})-r^{\star}(a_{-}))\|\sigma(r^{(t)}(a_{+})-r^{(t)}(a_{-}))\big)\leq\frac{C_{4}\alpha_{t}r_{\max}}{N_{t}(a_{+},a_{-})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of comparison for <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>
up to time <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. This motivates us to decompose <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> according
to whether <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}(a_{+},a_{-})\gg\alpha_{t}r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}(a_{+},a_{-})\gg\alpha_{t}r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>: let <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\coloneqq 100C_{4}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\coloneqq 100C_{4}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>
and denote by <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> the time of the <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th comparison
for <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\leq 2\tau A^{2}r_{\max}+\sum_{r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})}\underbrace{\sum_{n=\tau}^{N_{T}(a_{+},a_{-})}\big|r^{(t_{n})}(a_{+})-r^{(t_{n})}(a_{-})-r^{\star}(a_{+})+r^{\star}(a_{-})\big|}_{\eqqcolon\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\leq 2\tau A^{2}r_{\max}+\sum_{r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})}\underbrace{\sum_{n=\tau}^{N_{T}(a_{+},a_{-})}\big|r^{(t_{n})}(a_{+})-r^{(t_{n})}(a_{-})-r^{\star}(a_{+})+r^{\star}(a_{-})\big|}_{\eqqcolon\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where we denote by <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> the time of the <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th comparison
for <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the first summation is taken over all action
pairs <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>.
To bound each <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>, we need the following technical
lemma. The proof can be found in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof of auxiliary lemmas ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider any action pair <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>
and time <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t_{0}}(a_{+},a_{-})\geq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t_{0}}(a_{+},a_{-})\geq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists universal constant <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{5}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{5}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for
any <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\leq t_{1}&lt;t_{2}\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\leq t_{1}&lt;t_{2}\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability exceeding <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(T^{-10})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(T^{-10})</annotation></semantics></math>
we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N_{t_{2}}(a_{+},a_{-})-N_{t_{1}}(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N_{t_{2}}(a_{+},a_{-})-N_{t_{1}}(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{5}^{1/\beta}\sum_{t=t_{1}+1}^{t_{2}}\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\Big[\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+})-r^{\star}(a_{-}))\|\sigma(r^{(t)}(a_{+})-r^{(t)}(a_{-}))\big)^{\frac{1}{\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{5}^{1/\beta}\sum_{t=t_{1}+1}^{t_{2}}\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\Big[\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+})-r^{\star}(a_{-}))\|\sigma(r^{(t)}(a_{+})-r^{(t)}(a_{-}))\big)^{\frac{1}{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad+\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{-})-r^{\star}(a_{+}))^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\Big]+C_{5}\sqrt{T\log T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad+\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{-})-r^{\star}(a_{+}))^{\frac{1}{\beta}}\Big]+C_{5}\sqrt{T\log T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Equipped with Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 5.3 Step 3: bounding reward errors ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we can bound each <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>
using both density ratios regarding human feedback <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})/\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})/\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,
and regarding the reference policy <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proof of auxiliary lemmas ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists universal constant <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{6}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{6}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any action pair <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math>,
with probability exceeding <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-O(T^{-9})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-O(T^{-9})</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta(a_{+},a_{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{6}(r_{\max}+\log T)\min\left\{\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}},\left(T\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\right)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+1}}\alpha_{T}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}r_{\max}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{6}(r_{\max}+\log T)\min\left\{\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}},\left(T\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\right)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+1}}\alpha_{T}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}r_{\max}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+C_{6}\left(\frac{AN_{T}(a_{+},a_{-})\log T}{\alpha_{T}}+\sqrt{T\log T}\right)r_{\max}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+C_{6}\left(\frac{AN_{T}(a_{+},a_{-})\log T}{\alpha_{T}}+\sqrt{T\log T}\right)r_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This immediately implies that</p>
<table id="S5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\tau A^{2}r_{\max}+C_{6}\left(\frac{AT\log T}{\alpha_{T}}+A^{2}\sqrt{T\log T}\right)r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\tau A^{2}r_{\max}+C_{6}\left(\frac{AT\log T}{\alpha_{T}}+A^{2}\sqrt{T\log T}\right)r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+C_{6}(r_{\max}+\log T)\hskip-4.30554pt\sum_{r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})}\hskip-4.30554pt\min\bigg\{\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}},\left(T\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\right)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+1}}\alpha_{T}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}r_{\max}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}\bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖧𝖥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>T</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+C_{6}(r_{\max}+\log T)\hskip-4.30554pt\sum_{r^{\star}(a_{+})\geq r^{\star}(a_{-})}\hskip-4.30554pt\min\bigg\{\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{+})}{\pi_{\mathsf{HF}}(a_{-})}\alpha_{T}r_{\mathsf{max}},\left(T\frac{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{-})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{+})}\right)^{\frac{\beta}{\beta+1}}\alpha_{T}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}r_{\max}^{\frac{1}{\beta+1}}\bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Putting the regret decomposition (<a href="#S5.E3" title="In 5.1 Step 1: regret decomposition ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>) and the
bounds (<a href="#S5.E4" title="In 5.1 Step 1: regret decomposition ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>), (<a href="#S5.E5" title="In 5.2 Step 2: bounding likelihood ratios ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E9" title="In 5.3 Step 3: bounding reward errors ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a>)
collectively yields the desired regret bound (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 4 Theoretical results ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Discussion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we investigated the problem of efficient exploration in online RLHF. By a careful analysis of the existing optimism-based exploration strategies, we identified a conceptual drawback in their sampling protocol, and we proved lower bounds to show that they can lead to inefficient exploration. We then proposed our algorithm that explicitly targets uncertainty in reward differences most relevant for policy improvement. Under a multi-armed bandit setup of RLHF, we establish regret bounds of order <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{(\beta+1)/(\beta+2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{(\beta+1)/(\beta+2)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which scales polynomially in all model parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our work opens several avenues for future investigation. An immediate question is whether the rate <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{(\beta+1)/(\beta+2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{(\beta+1)/(\beta+2)}</annotation></semantics></math> is minimax optimal, or if faster rates can be achieved. Another important direction is to refine the dependence on parameters such as <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, which may be improved with sharper analysis or alternative exploration schemes. Finally, our theoretical results are restricted to the bandit setting; extending the analysis to richer environments that incorporate a prompt space would be an exciting step toward bridging theory and practice in online RLHF.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Acknowledgements</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">G. Li is supported in part by the Chinese University of Hong Kong Direct Grant for Research and the Hong Kong Research Grants Council ECS 2191363.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 Inadequacy of existing approaches ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> </h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, define the event</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}:=\{\text{no $a_{0}$ is sampled in the first $t$ samples}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>no </mtext><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> is sampled in the first </mtext><mi>t</mi><mtext> samples</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}:=\{\text{no $a_{0}$ is sampled in the first $t$ samples}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We will show that for any <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{t})\geq\frac{4}{9}\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{2(t-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{t})\geq\frac{4}{9}\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{2(t-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Conditional on <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be seen that <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math>
only depends on <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{1})-r(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{1})-r(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Now we study when we fix <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{1})-r(a_{2})\equiv\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{1})-r(a_{2})\equiv\delta</annotation></semantics></math>
such that <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, when is <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math>
maximized over both <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. By symmetry, we can assume without
loss of generality that <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. We can compute</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[r(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi}[r(a)]-\mathbb{E}_{a\sim\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}}[r(a)]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=[\pi(a_{1})-p][r(a_{1})-r(a_{0})]+[\pi(a_{2})-p][r(a_{2})-r(a_{0})]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[\pi(a_{1})-p][r(a_{1})-r(a_{0})]+[\pi(a_{2})-p][r(a_{2})-r(a_{0})]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=[\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})-2p][r(a_{1})-r(a_{0})]-\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})-2p][r(a_{1})-r(a_{0})]-\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For fixed <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, we check which reward function <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})&gt;2p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})&gt;2p</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=r_{\max}[\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})-2p]-\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r_{\max}[\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})-2p]-\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is maximized at <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{1})=r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{1})=r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{2})=r_{\max}-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{2})=r_{\max}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})&lt;2p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})&lt;2p</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(r_{\max}-\delta)[2p-\pi(a_{1})-\pi(a_{2})]-\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(r_{\max}-\delta)[2p-\pi(a_{1})-\pi(a_{2})]-\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is maximized at <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{1})=\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{1})=\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a_{0})=r_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a_{0})=r_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">In addition, for any policy <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})&lt;2p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a_{1})+\pi(a_{2})&lt;2p</annotation></semantics></math>,
by considering another policy <math id="A1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as <math id="A1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}(a_{1})=2p-\pi(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}(a_{1})=2p-\pi(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})=2p-\pi(a_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})=2p-\pi(a_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{r}J(\pi^{\prime},r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{r}J(\pi^{\prime},r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=r_{\max}[\pi^{\prime}(a_{1})+\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})-2p]-\delta[\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=r_{\max}[\pi^{\prime}(a_{1})+\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})-2p]-\delta[\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})-p]-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad-(r_{\max}-\delta)[2p-\pi(a_{1})-\pi(a_{2})]+\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]+\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad-(r_{\max}-\delta)[2p-\pi(a_{1})-\pi(a_{2})]+\delta[\pi(a_{2})-p]+\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\beta[\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\beta[\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Here the first relation follows from (<a href="#A1.E2" title="In 1st item ‣ Appendix A Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>), (<a href="#A1.E3" title="In 2nd item ‣ Appendix A Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>)
and the fact that <math id="A1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}(a_{1})+\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})&gt;2p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}(a_{1})+\pi^{\prime}(a_{2})&gt;2p</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\pi(a_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\pi(a_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\pi(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\pi(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\mathsf{KL}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x\log x+y\log y+(1-x-y)\log(1-x-y)-(2p-x)\log(2p-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x\log x+y\log y+(1-x-y)\log(1-x-y)-(2p-x)\log(2p-x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad-(2p-y)\log(2p-y)-(1-4p+x+y)\log(1+x+y-4p)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad-(2p-y)\log(2p-y)-(1-4p+x+y)\log(1+x+y-4p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">By elementary analysis, it is straightforward to check that <math id="A1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x,y)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x,y)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
for any <math id="A1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A1.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+y&lt;2p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+y&lt;2p</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{r}J(\pi^{\prime},r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})&gt;\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>r</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{r}J(\pi^{\prime},r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})&gt;\max_{r}J(\pi,r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore in order to maximize <math id="A1.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the following statement always holds regardless of the value of <math id="A1.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})=0,\quad\max\big\{r^{(t+1)}(a_{1}),r^{(t+1)}(a_{2})\big\}=r_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})=0,\quad\max\big\{r^{(t+1)}(a_{1}),r^{(t+1)}(a_{2})\big\}=r_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">This immediately implies that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})/\beta)}{\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})/\beta)+\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{1})/\beta)+\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{2})/\beta)}\leq\frac{1}{2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})/\beta)}{\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})/\beta)+\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{1})/\beta)+\exp(r^{(t+1)}(a_{2})/\beta)}\leq\frac{1}{2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">Therefore conditional on <math id="A1.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{t+1}|\mathcal{E}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{t+1}|\mathcal{E}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\big(1-\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})\big)^{2}\geq\left(\frac{1}{1+\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)}\right)^{2}\geq\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\big(1-\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})\big)^{2}\geq\left(\frac{1}{1+\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)}\right)^{2}\geq\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.9" class="ltx_p">This relation, together with</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{0})=\big(\pi^{(1)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(1)}(a_{2})\big)^{2}=\frac{4}{9}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{0})=\big(\pi^{(1)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(1)}(a_{2})\big)^{2}=\frac{4}{9},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.10" class="ltx_p">establishes the statement (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In Appendix A Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>). This immediately implies
that, for any <math id="A1.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)/2</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{t})\geq\frac{4}{9}\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{2(t-1)}\geq\frac{4}{9}\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}\geq\frac{4}{9e}\geq 0.16." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.16</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{t})\geq\frac{4}{9}\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{2(t-1)}\geq\frac{4}{9}\big(1-\exp(-r_{\max}/\beta)\big)^{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}\geq\frac{4}{9e}\geq 0.16.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, when <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> holds, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi^{\star}(a_{0})-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\star}\|\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})+\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{(t)}\|\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi^{\star}(a_{0})-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\star}\|\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})+\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{(t)}\|\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}(a_{0})=\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2},\quad\pi^{\star}(a_{1})=\pi^{\star}(a_{2})=\frac{1}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}(a_{0})=\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2},\quad\pi^{\star}(a_{1})=\pi^{\star}(a_{2})=\frac{1}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\star}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\star}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log 3+\pi^{\star}(a_{0})\log\pi^{\star}(a_{0})+\pi^{\star}(a_{1})\log\pi^{\star}(a_{1})+\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\log\pi^{\star}(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log 3+\pi^{\star}(a_{0})\log\pi^{\star}(a_{0})+\pi^{\star}(a_{1})\log\pi^{\star}(a_{1})+\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\log\pi^{\star}(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log 3+\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}\log\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}+\frac{2}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}\log\frac{1}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log 3+\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}\log\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}+\frac{2}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}\log\frac{1}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log 3+\beta^{-1}\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}-\log[\exp(1/\beta)+2]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log 3+\beta^{-1}\frac{\exp(1/\beta)}{\exp(1/\beta)+2}-\log[\exp(1/\beta)+2].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">In addition, when <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> happens, we know that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{(t)}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{(t)}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log 3+\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log 3+\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{(i)}}{\geq}\log 3+\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})+\big[\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})\big]\log\frac{\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(i)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{(i)}}{\geq}\log 3+\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})+\big[\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})\big]\log\frac{\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})+\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log 3+\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})+\big[1-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\big]\log\frac{1-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log 3+\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\log\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})+\big[1-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\big]\log\frac{1-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}\log 3-\log 2-0.16." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(ii)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.16</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}\log 3-\log 2-0.16.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Here step (i) uses Jensen’s inequality for convex function <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=x\log x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=x\log x</annotation></semantics></math>;
step (ii) holds since the function <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=x\log x+(1-x)\log(1-x)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=x\log x+(1-x)\log(1-x)/2</annotation></semantics></math>
is monotonically decreasing for <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;x&lt;1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;x&lt;1/3</annotation></semantics></math>, and we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\leq\frac{1}{2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}\leq\frac{1}{2+\exp(3)}\leq 0.046" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.046</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\leq\frac{1}{2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}\leq\frac{1}{2+\exp(3)}\leq 0.046</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">provided that <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}/\beta\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}/\beta\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝖼𝖺𝗅</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{cal}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi^{\star}(a_{0})-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\star}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})+\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{(t)}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi^{\star}(a_{0})-\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})-\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{\star}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})+\beta\mathsf{KL}(\pi^{(t)}\parallel\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\beta\log\big(\exp(1/\beta)+2\big)-(\log 2+0.16)\beta-0.046" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.046</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\beta\log\big(\exp(1/\beta)+2\big)-(\log 2+0.16)\beta-0.046</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1/2," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1/2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.7" class="ltx_p">where the last relation holds for any <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3.2 Our approach: exploration based on uncertainty ‣ 3 RLHF with online exploration ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> </h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\min\{\kappa,\exp(r_{\max})/2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\min\{\kappa,\exp(r_{\max})/2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the events</p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}\coloneqq\big\{a_{2}^{t}=a_{0}\text{ for all }1\leq t\leq T\big\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext> for all </mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\coloneqq\big\{a_{2}^{t}=a_{0}\text{ for all }1\leq t\leq T\big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{E}:=\{a_{1}^{t}\succ a_{2}^{t}\text{ or }a_{1}^{t}=a_{2}^{t}\text{ for all }1\leq t\leq T\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mtext> or </mtext><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mtext> for all </mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}:=\{a_{1}^{t}\succ a_{2}^{t}\text{ or }a_{1}^{t}=a_{2}^{t}\text{ for all }1\leq t\leq T\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We can check that when <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{A})=[\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{0})]^{T}\leq(1-2\kappa^{-1})^{\kappa}\geq\frac{1}{16}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{A})=[\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{0})]^{T}\leq(1-2\kappa^{-1})^{\kappa}\geq\frac{1}{16}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Conditional on <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that when <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}\,|\,\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}\,|\,\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\Big(\frac{\exp(r_{\max}-1)}{1+\exp(r_{\max}-1)}\Big)^{T}\geq\Big(\frac{\exp(r_{\max}-1)}{1+\exp(r_{\max}-1)}\Big)^{\exp(r_{\max})/2}\geq\frac{1}{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\Big(\frac{\exp(r_{\max}-1)}{1+\exp(r_{\max}-1)}\Big)^{T}\geq\Big(\frac{\exp(r_{\max}-1)}{1+\exp(r_{\max}-1)}\Big)^{\exp(r_{\max})/2}\geq\frac{1}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Conditional on <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq T-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
all the preference data in <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> are of form <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}^{t}\succ a_{2}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}^{t}\succ a_{2}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this case, it is straightforward to check that the reward function
that maximizes <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(r,\mathcal{D}^{(t)})+\alpha J^{\star}(r;\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>
is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})=0,\quad r^{(t+1)}(a_{1})=r^{(t+1)}(a_{2})=r_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(t+1)}(a_{0})=0,\quad r^{(t+1)}(a_{1})=r^{(t+1)}(a_{2})=r_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This immediately implies that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})=\frac{\kappa-2}{\kappa-2+2\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)},\quad\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{1})=\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{2})=\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{\kappa-2+2\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{0})=\frac{\kappa-2}{\kappa-2+2\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)},\quad\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{1})=\pi^{(t+1)}(a_{2})=\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{\kappa-2+2\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, we know that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa-2}{\kappa-2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)+\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa-2}{\kappa-2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)+\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(a_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(a_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{\kappa-2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)+\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{\kappa-2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)+\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\star}(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)}{\kappa-2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)+\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)}{\kappa-2+\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)+\exp((r_{\max}-2)/\beta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.8" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, we first lower bound</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\geq J(\pi_{\theta^{\star}};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi_{1};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\geq J(\pi_{\theta^{\star}};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi_{1};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.9" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, where we define <math id="A2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}\coloneqq\theta\pi^{(t)}+(1-\theta)\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}\coloneqq\theta\pi^{(t)}+(1-\theta)\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the above relation follows from the optimality of <math id="A2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall the definition</p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi;r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi;r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi(a_{1})r_{\max}+\pi(a_{2})(r_{\max}-2)-\beta\sum_{i=0}^{2}\pi(a_{i})\log\frac{\pi(a_{i})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{i})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi(a_{1})r_{\max}+\pi(a_{2})(r_{\max}-2)-\beta\sum_{i=0}^{2}\pi(a_{i})\log\frac{\pi(a_{i})}{\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{i})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.10" class="ltx_p">we can compute</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\pi}J(\pi;r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})=\left[\begin{array}[]{c}r^{\star}(a_{0})-\beta\log[\pi(a_{0})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{0})]-\beta\\
r^{\star}(a_{1})-\beta\log[\pi(a_{1})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{1})]-\beta\\
r^{\star}(a_{2})-\beta\log[\pi(a_{2})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{2})]-\beta\end{array}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>π</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\pi}J(\pi;r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})=\left[\begin{array}[]{c}r^{\star}(a_{0})-\beta\log[\pi(a_{0})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{0})]-\beta\\
r^{\star}(a_{1})-\beta\log[\pi(a_{1})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{1})]-\beta\\
r^{\star}(a_{2})-\beta\log[\pi(a_{2})/\pi_{\mathsf{ref}}(a_{2})]-\beta\end{array}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.11" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\pi}^{2}J(\pi;r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})=-\beta\mathsf{diag}\left\{\pi(a_{0}),\pi(a_{1}),\pi(a_{2})\right\}^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝖺𝗀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\pi}^{2}J(\pi;r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})=-\beta\mathsf{diag}\left\{\pi(a_{0}),\pi(a_{1}),\pi(a_{2})\right\}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.12" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to check that</p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\pi}J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})=\left[\begin{array}[]{c}0\\
0\\
-1\end{array}\right]+\mathsf{const}\cdot\left[\begin{array}[]{c}1\\
1\\
1\end{array}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>π</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖼𝗈𝗇𝗌𝗍</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="2.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\pi}J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})=\left[\begin{array}[]{c}0\\
0\\
-1\end{array}\right]+\mathsf{const}\cdot\left[\begin{array}[]{c}1\\
1\\
1\end{array}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})&lt;\pi^{\star}(a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})&lt;\pi^{\star}(a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})&lt;\pi^{\star}(a_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})&lt;\pi^{\star}(a_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})&gt;\pi^{\star}(a_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})&gt;\pi^{\star}(a_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that for any <math id="A2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in[0,\theta^{\star}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in[0,\theta^{\star}]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\pi}^{2}J(\pi_{\theta};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\pi}^{2}J(\pi_{\theta};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\succeq-\beta\mathsf{diag}\big\{\pi^{(t)}(a_{0}),\pi^{(t)}(a_{1}),\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})+(1-\theta^{\star})\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\big\}^{-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝖺𝗀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\succeq-\beta\mathsf{diag}\big\{\pi^{(t)}(a_{0}),\pi^{(t)}(a_{1}),\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})+(1-\theta^{\star})\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\big\}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Therefore we have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi_{\theta^{\star}};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi_{1};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\overset{\text{(i)}}{\geq}\theta^{\star}\nabla_{\pi}J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})^{\top}(\pi^{\star}-\pi^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(i)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>π</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi_{\theta^{\star}};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi_{1};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\overset{\text{(i)}}{\geq}\theta^{\star}\nabla_{\pi}J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})^{\top}(\pi^{\star}-\pi^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}(\pi^{\star}-\pi^{(t)})^{\top}\mathsf{diag}\big\{\pi^{(t)}(a_{0}),\pi^{(t)}(a_{1}),\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})+(1-\theta^{\star})\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\big\}^{-1}(\pi^{\star}-\pi^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖽𝗂𝖺𝗀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}(\pi^{\star}-\pi^{(t)})^{\top}\mathsf{diag}\big\{\pi^{(t)}(a_{0}),\pi^{(t)}(a_{1}),\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})+(1-\theta^{\star})\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\big\}^{-1}(\pi^{\star}-\pi^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}\theta^{\star}[\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\pi^{\star}(a_{2})]-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}[\pi^{\star}(a_{0})+\pi^{\star}(a_{1})+\frac{9}{16}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})/\theta^{\star}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(ii)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\overset{\text{(ii)}}{\geq}\theta^{\star}[\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\pi^{\star}(a_{2})]-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}[\pi^{\star}(a_{0})+\pi^{\star}(a_{1})+\frac{9}{16}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})/\theta^{\star}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\theta^{\star}[\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\pi^{\star}(a_{2})]-\frac{9}{32}\beta\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}[1-\pi^{\star}(a_{2})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\theta^{\star}[\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\pi^{\star}(a_{2})]-\frac{9}{32}\beta\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}[1-\pi^{\star}(a_{2})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\left(1-\frac{9}{32}\beta\right)\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\left(1-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star}}{2}\right)\theta^{\star}\pi^{\star}(a_{2})-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\left(1-\frac{9}{32}\beta\right)\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\left(1-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star}}{2}\right)\theta^{\star}\pi^{\star}(a_{2})-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\overset{\text{(iii)}}{\geq}\left(\frac{3}{4}-\frac{9}{32}\beta+\frac{\beta\theta^{\star}}{8}\right)\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}\overset{\text{(iv)}}{\geq}\frac{15}{32}\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\frac{\theta^{\star 2}}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(iii)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">(iv)</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>15</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\overset{\text{(iii)}}{\geq}\left(\frac{3}{4}-\frac{9}{32}\beta+\frac{\beta\theta^{\star}}{8}\right)\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\frac{\beta\theta^{\star 2}}{2}\overset{\text{(iv)}}{\geq}\frac{15}{32}\theta^{\star}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})-\frac{\theta^{\star 2}}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.15" class="ltx_p">Here step (i) follows from the Taylor expansion and (<a href="#A2.E3" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>);
step (ii) utilizes (<a href="#A2.E2" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>) and as well as the following
relations</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\leq\pi^{\star}(a_{0})\leq 2\pi^{(t)}(a_{0}),\quad\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})\leq\pi^{\star}(a_{1})\leq 2\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}(a_{0})\leq\pi^{\star}(a_{0})\leq 2\pi^{(t)}(a_{0}),\quad\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})\leq\pi^{\star}(a_{1})\leq 2\pi^{(t)}(a_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.16" class="ltx_p">and when <math id="A2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\leq\frac{2}{\exp(2/\beta)+1}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})\leq\frac{1}{4}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2});" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}(a_{2})\leq\frac{2}{\exp(2/\beta)+1}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})\leq\frac{1}{4}\pi^{(t)}(a_{2});</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.17" class="ltx_p">steps (iii) and (iv) follows from (<a href="#A2.E5" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>) and <math id="A2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\leq\exp(r_{\max}\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\leq\exp(r_{\max}\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})=\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{\kappa-2+2\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}\geq\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{3\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)-2}\geq\frac{1}{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(t)}(a_{2})=\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{\kappa-2+2\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}\geq\frac{\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)}{3\exp(r_{\max}/\beta)-2}\geq\frac{1}{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.18" class="ltx_p">By taking (<a href="#A2.E1" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>), (<a href="#A2.E4" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>)
collectively, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\geq\frac{5}{32}\theta^{\star}-\frac{\theta^{\star 2}}{2}\geq\frac{25}{2048}&gt;0.01" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝗋𝖾𝖿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>32</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>2048</mn></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi^{\star};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})-J(\pi^{(t)};r^{\star},\pi_{\mathsf{ref}})\geq\frac{5}{32}\theta^{\star}-\frac{\theta^{\star 2}}{2}\geq\frac{25}{2048}&gt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.19" class="ltx_p">where we take <math id="A2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\star}=5/32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\star}=5/32</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of auxiliary lemmas</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 5.2 Step 2: bounding likelihood ratios ‣ 5 Proof of Theorem ‣ Towards Efficient Online Exploration for Reinforcement Learning with Human Feedback" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first express</p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{i}\coloneqq\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{-}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{+}^{i})-r(a_{-}^{i}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{i}\coloneqq\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{+}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{-}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{+}^{i})-r(a_{-}^{i}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\ind\{a_{1}^{i}\succ a_{2}^{i}\}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))}+\ind\{a_{1}^{i}\prec a_{2}^{i}\}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{2}^{i})-r(a_{1}^{i}))}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>𝟙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≺</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ind\{a_{1}^{i}\succ a_{2}^{i}\}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))}+\ind\{a_{1}^{i}\prec a_{2}^{i}\}\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{2}^{i})-r(a_{1}^{i}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It is straightforward to check that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[X_{i}\big|a_{1}^{i},a_{2}^{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[X_{i}\big|a_{1}^{i},a_{2}^{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\left(a_{1}^{i}\succ a_{2}^{i}|a_{1}^{i},a_{2}^{i}\right)\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))}+\mathbb{P}\left(a_{1}^{i}\prec a_{2}^{i}|a_{1}^{i},a_{2}^{i}\right)\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{2}^{i})-r(a_{1}^{i}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≺</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}\left(a_{1}^{i}\succ a_{2}^{i}|a_{1}^{i},a_{2}^{i}\right)\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))}+\mathbb{P}\left(a_{1}^{i}\prec a_{2}^{i}|a_{1}^{i},a_{2}^{i}\right)\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{2}^{i})-r(a_{1}^{i}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))}+\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{2}^{i})-r(a_{1}^{i}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))}+\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))\log\frac{\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i}))}{\sigma(r(a_{2}^{i})-r(a_{1}^{i}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{KL}\big(\sigma(r^{\star}(a_{1}^{i})-r^{\star}(a_{2}^{i}))\parallel\sigma(r(a_{1}^{i})-r(a_{2}^{i}))\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|X_{i}\right|\leq\left|\log\left(1+\exp(-r(a_{+}^{i})+r(a_{-}^{i}))\right)\right|\leq 2r_{\mathsf{max}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗆𝖺𝗑</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|X_{i}\right|\leq\left|\log\left(1+\exp(-r(a_{+}^{i})+r(a_{-}^{i}))\right)\right|\leq 2r_{\mathsf{max}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">In addition, we can compute the variance</p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
